# SQLC Type Safety Patterns

## Critical Type Safety Rules

### 1. Always Cast CASE Expressions
❌ **NEVER write CASE without explicit casting:**
```sql
CASE WHEN condition THEN value ELSE NULL END  -- Generates interface{}
```

✅ **ALWAYS cast CASE expressions:**
```sql
CASE WHEN condition THEN value ELSE NULL END::text  -- Generates string
CASE WHEN condition THEN value ELSE NULL END::varchar  -- Generates string
```

**Why:** sqlc loses type information with CASE expressions ([issue #2937](https://github.com/sqlc-dev/sqlc/issues/2937))

### 2. Use Named Arguments  
✅ **Prefer named arguments:**
```sql
sqlc.arg(field_name)     -- Required field
sqlc.narg(field_name)    -- Nullable field  
```

❌ **Avoid positional arguments:**
```sql
$1, $2, $3  -- Hard to maintain, error-prone
```

### 3. Column Overrides in sqlc.yaml
For nullable PII fields, add column overrides in [`sqlc.yaml`](mdc:packages/database/sqlc.yaml):

```yaml
overrides:
  # Authentication credentials nullable fields
  - column: "authentication_credentials.google_connector_ref"
    go_type: "pgtype.Text"
  - column: "profiles.first_name"
    go_type: "pgtype.Text"
```

## Expected Go Types

### Parameters (Input)
```go
// Nullable PII fields should use pgtype.Text
GoogleConnectorRef  pgtype.Text `json:"google_connector_ref"`
FirstName          pgtype.Text `json:"first_name"`

// Required fields use primitive types
PublicKey          string      `json:"public_key"`
```

### Return Values (Output)
```go
// Decrypted PII fields should be string (not interface{})  
GoogleConnectorRef  string `json:"google_connector_ref"`
FirstName          string `json:"first_name"`
```

## Common Patterns

### UPDATE with Conditional Encryption
```sql
UPDATE table SET 
    pii_field = CASE 
        WHEN sqlc.narg(pii_field) IS NOT NULL 
        THEN pgp_sym_encrypt(sqlc.narg(pii_field), sqlc.arg(encryption_key))
        ELSE pii_field  -- Keep existing value
    END::varchar
```

### SELECT with Conditional Decryption
```sql
SELECT 
    CASE 
        WHEN pii_field IS NOT NULL 
        THEN pgp_sym_decrypt(pii_field::bytea, sqlc.arg(encryption_key))
        ELSE NULL 
    END::text as pii_field
FROM table;
```

## Testing Type Generation

After changes, always verify:
1. `bun db:generate`
2. Check generated Go structs have proper types (no `interface{}`)
3. Ensure nullable fields use `pgtype.Text` for parameters